---
import ServiceLayout from '../../layouts/ServiceLayout.astro';
import { breadcrumbSchema, faqSchema } from '../../utils/schema';

const SITE_URL = 'https://elan-tech.net';

const faqs = [
  {
    question: 'What should I look for in ADA website remediation providers?',
    answer: 'The best ADA website remediation providers share three traits: (1) code-level fixes, not overlay widgets — 22.64% of sites sued in 2025 already had an accessibility widget installed, and the FTC fined accessiBe $1 million for misleading compliance claims; (2) WCAG 2.1 AA conformance testing with documented VPAT/ACR reports your attorney can submit as evidence of a good-faith remediation effort; (3) fast turnaround — emergency audits within 24 hours when a demand-letter deadline is on the clock. eLan Technology is an ADA website remediation provider offering exactly this: 24-hour emergency audits, fixed pricing from $1,500, full code-level remediation, and VPAT documentation — at 60-70% less than the $15,000-$50,000 typically charged by US accessibility agencies.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What is the ADA website compliance checklist?',
    answer: 'An ADA website compliance checklist is the practical set of fixes that brings a site in line with WCAG 2.1 Level AA — the standard US courts treat as the benchmark for ADA Title III. In plain English, the checklist boils down to: every image needs alt text, every form field needs a label, text needs at least 4.5:1 contrast against its background, every interactive element must work with a keyboard alone, focus indicators must be visible, headings must follow a logical order, the page language must be declared, and any video needs captions or a transcript. Six of these account for 96% of all real-world lawsuits — low contrast, missing alt text, missing form labels, empty links, missing document language, and empty buttons. We publish a deeper walkthrough in our <a href="/blog/accessibility/ada-compliance-checklist/">ADA compliance checklist guide</a>, and our audit hands you the same checklist scored against your live pages.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What are the ADA compliance requirements for a website in 2026?',
    answer: 'There is no single federal statute that says "your website must meet X" — instead, ADA Title III says public accommodations must be accessible, and the DOJ + federal courts have made WCAG 2.1 Level AA the de facto technical bar. Practically, that means your site needs to be perceivable (alt text, captions, contrast), operable (keyboard-friendly, no seizure triggers, enough time to read), understandable (clear labels, predictable navigation, helpful errors), and robust (clean semantic HTML that assistive tech can parse). The DOJ\'s April 24, 2026 Title II rule formalised WCAG 2.1 AA for state and local governments — and that decision is the standard plaintiff attorneys are already citing in private-sector cases.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What are the WCAG 2.1 AA standards?',
    answer: 'WCAG 2.1 (Web Content Accessibility Guidelines) is published by the W3C and organised under four principles — Perceivable, Operable, Understandable, Robust, abbreviated POUR. Each principle breaks down into success criteria, rated A (basic), AA (industry standard), or AAA (gold standard). The WCAG 2.1 AA accessibility standards add 50 testable criteria covering text contrast, resize behaviour, keyboard traps, focus visibility, error identification, language of parts, and more. AA is the conformance level cited by the ADA, Section 508, the European Accessibility Act, and most procurement contracts. We break the criteria down without jargon in our <a href="/blog/accessibility/wcag-explained-business-owners/">WCAG explained for business owners</a> post.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What are the actual requirements for an ADA-compliant website?',
    answer: 'Stripped of legalese, ADA-compliant website requirements are: (1) every meaningful image carries descriptive alt text; (2) every form input has a programmatically associated label and clear error messaging; (3) all functionality works with keyboard alone — no mouse required; (4) text contrast is at least 4.5:1 for body copy and 3:1 for large text; (5) focus is always visible and follows a logical order; (6) headings (H1, H2, H3) describe the page structure honestly; (7) page language is declared in the HTML; (8) audio and video have captions or transcripts; (9) nothing flashes more than three times per second; (10) users have enough time to read and interact, with no auto-advancing carousels that can\'t be paused. A WCAG 2.1 AA audit verifies all of this against your live site and tells you exactly what to fix.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Is there a free way to check my site against the ADA compliance checklist?',
    answer: 'Yes — start with a quick automated scan. Tools like axe DevTools, WAVE, and Google Lighthouse will flag the most obvious violations in a few minutes (missing alt text, low contrast, empty buttons). They are good for a first pass but typically catch only 30–40% of issues; the rest — keyboard traps, focus order, screen-reader logic, form-error flows — require manual testing by someone trained in WCAG. That is the gap our <a href="/free-website-audit/">free website audit</a> closes: a real human runs the checklist against your homepage and three key pages, and gives you a plain-English report with the priorities ranked. If you want the full WCAG 2.1 AA audit across every page with VPAT documentation, that starts at $1,500.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Is my website required to be ADA compliant?',
    answer: 'If your business serves US customers, yes. ADA Title III applies to "places of public accommodation," and US courts have consistently ruled that websites qualify. In 2025 alone, 5,100+ digital accessibility lawsuits were filed — and 67% targeted businesses with under $25M in annual revenue. Any business with a website that serves the US can be a target.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What is WCAG 2.1 Level AA?',
    answer: 'WCAG 2.1 Level AA is the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines published by the W3C, at the AA conformance level. It is the de facto technical standard the DOJ and US courts reference for ADA website compliance. It covers text contrast, alt text, keyboard navigation, form labels, focus indicators, captions, and many other criteria designed to make websites usable by people with disabilities.',
  },
  {
    question: 'How much does ADA website compliance cost?',
    answer: 'At eLan Technology, an ADA compliance audit starts at $1,500 USD. Audit + remediation projects typically range from $3,000-$8,000. A new ADA-compliant website from scratch costs $3,000-$12,000. Compare this to an average ADA settlement of $30,000 (out-of-court), $85,000 (judgment), or $400,000 (class action) — compliance is dramatically cheaper than litigation.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Can I be sued if my website isn\'t accessible?',
    answer: 'Yes. 5,100+ ADA digital accessibility lawsuits were filed in 2025, a 37% increase over 2024. New York alone accounted for 1,021 federal filings. eCommerce sites are the most common target (69-77% of cases), but any business with a website serving US customers can be sued — including small businesses with under $25M in revenue.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Do accessibility widgets or overlays make my site ADA compliant?',
    answer: 'No. In 2025, 22.64% of ADA lawsuits targeted websites that already had accessibility widgets installed. The FTC fined accessiBe $1 million for misleading compliance claims. Overlays cannot fix underlying code-level violations. Only proper code-level remediation — the work eLan Technology delivers — provides genuine compliance and legal protection.',
  },
  {
    question: 'How long does it take to make a website ADA compliant?',
    answer: 'For an existing site, audit + remediation typically takes 2-6 weeks depending on site size and the number of violations found. For a new website built ADA-compliant from day one, no extra time is needed — accessibility is part of our standard development process. We deliver audit reports within 24 hours of starting.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What happens if I receive an ADA demand letter?',
    answer: 'Do not ignore it. Demand letters often settle for around $5,000 if you respond quickly and demonstrate a remediation plan. Contact a qualified accessibility consultant immediately, conduct an audit, and begin remediation. eLan Technology can provide an emergency audit and remediation plan within 24-48 hours to support your legal response.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Does eLan Technology provide VPAT documentation?',
    answer: 'Yes. We provide VPAT (Voluntary Product Accessibility Template) and ACR (Accessibility Conformance Report) documentation as part of our ADA compliance package. These documents describe how your website conforms to WCAG 2.1 AA and are often required for government contracts, B2B sales, and legal defence.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Can you audit my existing website for ADA compliance?',
    answer: 'Yes. Our ADA compliance audit scans every page of your site against WCAG 2.1 AA, identifies the top 10 critical violations, ranks them by priority, and provides a remediation cost estimate. Audits start at $1,500 USD; results are delivered within 24 hours. Contact us to get started.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What is the DOJ Title II April 2026 deadline?',
    answer: 'On April 24, 2026, the DOJ\'s Title II final rule takes full effect, requiring state and local governments (and their contractors) to meet WCAG 2.1 AA on all public-facing digital content. While Title II targets the public sector, it sets the definitive technical standard that courts will continue to reference for private-sector ADA Title III cases.',
  },
];

const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', href: '/' },
  { name: 'Services', href: '/services/' },
  { name: 'ADA-Compliant Web Design', href: '/services/ada-compliant-web-design/' },
];

const serviceSchemaObj = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Service',
  name: 'ADA Website Remediation',
  alternateName: 'ADA-Compliant Web Design',
  description:
    'ADA website remediation and WCAG 2.1 AA compliant website design and development services that protect US businesses from ADA website lawsuits.',
  url: `${SITE_URL}/services/ada-compliant-web-design/`,
  provider: {
    '@type': 'Organization',
    name: 'eLan Technology',
    url: SITE_URL,
  },
  areaServed: {
    '@type': 'Country',
    name: 'United States',
  },
  serviceType: 'Website Accessibility Compliance',
  offers: {
    '@type': 'Offer',
    price: '1500',
    priceCurrency: 'USD',
    description: 'ADA compliance audit starting price',
  },
};

const schemaBreadcrumbs = breadcrumbs.map(b => ({ name: b.name, url: b.href }));
const schemas = [serviceSchemaObj, faqSchema(faqs), breadcrumbSchema(schemaBreadcrumbs)];
---
<ServiceLayout
  title="ADA Website Remediation Providers | WCAG 2.1 AA Audit & Fix | eLan Technology"
  description="Facing an ADA demand letter? Trusted ADA website remediation — WCAG 2.1 AA code-level audit, emergency 24-hr turnaround, VPAT documentation. Fixed price from $1,500. Free consult."
  canonical="/services/ada-compliant-web-design/"
  schema={schemas}
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
>

    <!-- ── HERO ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="service-card relative mb-12 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-[var(--border)] p-8 md:p-12" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, color-mix(in srgb, var(--ac-blue) 12%, var(--bg-card)) 0%, var(--bg-card) 65%);">
    <span aria-hidden="true" class="service-card__num pointer-events-none absolute top-4 right-6 font-heading font-black leading-none select-none" style="color: var(--ac-blue); font-size: 7rem;">10</span>
    <span aria-hidden="true" class="service-card__stripe pointer-events-none absolute -left-12 -bottom-12 h-60 w-60 rotate-[-20deg] opacity-[0.08]" style="background: var(--ac-blue);"></span>
    <div class="relative">
      <p class="mb-3 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-red-500">Emergency ADA Remediation — 24-Hour Response</p>
      <h1 class="font-heading text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-[var(--text)] md:text-5xl">
        Facing an ADA Digital Accessibility Lawsuit? We Specialise in Immediate Website Remediation
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-3xl text-base text-[var(--text-muted)] md:text-lg">
        5,100+ ADA digital accessibility lawsuits were filed in 2025 — a 37% increase YoY. If you've received a demand letter or court summons, eLan Technology provides emergency WCAG 2.2 AA audits within 24 hours and full code-level remediation to support your legal defence, including VPAT documentation.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-7 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a href="/get-quote/?service=ada-emergency" class="inline-flex items-center rounded-lg bg-red-500 px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-semibold text-white shadow transition hover:bg-red-600">
          Emergency ADA Audit — 24hr Response
        </a>
        <a href="/get-quote" class="inline-flex items-center rounded-lg border border-[var(--border)] px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--text)] transition hover:bg-[var(--bg)]">
          Get a Quote
        </a>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-[var(--text-muted)]">
        On a lawsuit or demand-letter deadline? See our <a href="/services/ada-compliant-web-design/emergency-remediation/" class="font-semibold text-red-500 underline hover:no-underline">emergency / deadline remediation</a> — Shopify &amp; ecommerce sites fixed in under 30 days.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

    <!-- ── INTRO: HUMANISED CONTEXT ────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="mb-16 max-w-3xl">
      <p class="text-base text-[var(--text-muted)] md:text-lg leading-relaxed mb-4">
        ADA compliance for a website sounds like a legal puzzle, but it really comes down to one thing: can a person who can't see a screen, can't use a mouse, or processes information differently still use your site? If the answer is yes, you've already met the spirit of the law. The work is in proving it, page by page, against a checklist the courts actually recognise — and that checklist is <a href="/blog/accessibility/wcag-explained-business-owners/" class="text-red-500 underline hover:no-underline">WCAG 2.1 Level AA</a>.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base text-[var(--text-muted)] md:text-lg leading-relaxed mb-4">
        We've built websites for 24 years. Accessibility isn't a service line we bolted on when lawsuits started trending — it's how we've shipped sites since 2002. What's changed in the last two years is the speed and scale of enforcement: AI tools let any plaintiff file a competent complaint in minutes, automated scanners crawl thousands of sites a night, and 67% of new cases now target small businesses, not Fortune 500s.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base text-[var(--text-muted)] md:text-lg leading-relaxed">
        If you're researching what compliance actually requires — start with our <a href="/blog/accessibility/ada-compliance-checklist/" class="text-red-500 underline hover:no-underline">plain-English ADA compliance checklist</a>. If you've already received a demand letter, skip to the emergency section below — every day matters.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- ── SECTION 1: LAWSUIT CRISIS ───────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="mb-16">
      <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl font-bold text-[var(--text)] md:text-3xl mb-4">5,100+ ADA Website Lawsuits in 2025 — Is Your Business Next?</h2>
      <p class="text-[var(--text-muted)] mb-6">The numbers tell a stark story. ADA digital accessibility litigation has exploded — and small businesses are now the primary target, not just Fortune 500 corporations.</p>

      <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 mb-8">
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-red-500/30 bg-red-500/5 p-5">
          <p class="font-heading text-3xl font-bold text-red-500">5,100+</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-[var(--text-muted)]">Digital accessibility lawsuits filed in 2025</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-red-500/30 bg-red-500/5 p-5">
          <p class="font-heading text-3xl font-bold text-red-500">+37%</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-[var(--text-muted)]">Year-over-year increase (EcomBack 2025 report)</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-red-500/30 bg-red-500/5 p-5">
          <p class="font-heading text-3xl font-bold text-red-500">67%</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-[var(--text-muted)]">Of lawsuits target businesses under $25M revenue</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-red-500/30 bg-red-500/5 p-5">
          <p class="font-heading text-3xl font-bold text-red-500">$30K</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-[var(--text-muted)]">Average out-of-court ADA settlement</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h3 class="font-heading text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text)] mb-3">Top States by Filing Volume (2025)</h3>
      <ul class="grid gap-2 sm:grid-cols-2 mb-8 text-sm text-[var(--text-muted)]" role="list">
        <li class="rounded-lg border border-[var(--border)] bg-[var(--bg-card)] px-4 py-2"><strong class="text-[var(--text)]">New York:</strong> 1,021 lawsuits (33% of all federal filings)</li>
        <li class="rounded-lg border border-[var(--border)] bg-[var(--bg-card)] px-4 py-2"><strong class="text-[var(--text)]">Florida:</strong> 487 lawsuits (nearly doubled YoY)</li>
        <li class="rounded-lg border border-[var(--border)] bg-[var(--bg-card)] px-4 py-2"><strong class="text-[var(--text)]">California:</strong> 380 lawsuits</li>
        <li class="rounded-lg border border-[var(--border)] bg-[var(--bg-card)] px-4 py-2"><strong class="text-[var(--text)]">Illinois:</strong> 237 lawsuits (746% increase YoY)</li>
      </ul>

      <h3 class="font-heading text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text)] mb-3">The AI Factor — Why Lawsuits Are Exploding</h3>
      <p class="text-[var(--text-muted)] mb-4">Pro se filings (individuals filing without attorneys) increased 40% in 2025. AI tools like ChatGPT now allow anyone to draft a competent ADA complaint in minutes. The barrier to filing a lawsuit has essentially disappeared — and plaintiff law firms have built automated scanning tools that find violations on thousands of websites overnight.</p>

      <h3 class="font-heading text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text)] mb-3">The Widget Myth</h3>
      <p class="text-[var(--text-muted)] mb-4">22.64% of ADA lawsuits in 2025 targeted websites that already had accessibility widgets installed. The FTC fined accessiBe $1 million for misleading compliance claims. Overlays and widgets do not prevent lawsuits — only code-level remediation provides real protection.</p>

      <div class="rounded-xl border border-red-500/30 bg-red-500/5 p-5">
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--text)]">Don't wait for a demand letter. <a href="/get-quote" class="text-red-500 underline hover:no-underline">Request your ADA compliance audit today →</a></p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── SECTION 1b: EMERGENCY — ALREADY SUED ─────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="mb-16">
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-red-500/40 bg-red-500/5 p-8 md:p-10">
        <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl font-bold text-[var(--text)] md:text-3xl mb-4">Already Received an ADA Demand Letter or Lawsuit? Here's What to Do Right Now</h2>
        <p class="text-[var(--text-muted)] mb-6">An ADA demand letter is time-sensitive. Ignoring it turns a $5,000 settlement into a $30,000–$85,000 judgment. Here is the immediate action plan recommended by accessibility specialists.</p>

        <ol class="space-y-4 mb-8">
          {[
            { step: '1', title: 'Do not ignore the letter', desc: 'Demand letters typically give 30–60 days to respond. Failure to respond escalates to a federal court filing automatically.' },
            { step: '2', title: 'Engage an accessibility specialist immediately', desc: 'You need an audit to demonstrate a good-faith remediation effort — this is your primary legal defence. eLan Technology delivers emergency audits within 24 hours.' },
            { step: '3', title: 'Request an emergency WCAG audit', desc: 'The audit identifies every violation, prioritised by severity, with code-level fixes. This becomes the evidence of your remediation plan for your attorney.' },
            { step: '4', title: 'Begin remediation — even partially', desc: 'Courts and plaintiff attorneys consider active remediation a mitigating factor. Starting work immediately — even before completion — significantly reduces settlement risk.' },
            { step: '5', title: 'Obtain VPAT documentation', desc: 'A Voluntary Product Accessibility Template (VPAT / ACR) is the formal document proving compliance. eLan Technology provides this with every audit package.' },
          ].map(({ step, title, desc }) => (
            <li class="flex gap-4">
              <span class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-red-500 text-white text-sm font-bold flex items-center justify-center">{step}</span>
              <div>
                <p class="font-semibold text-[var(--text)]">{title}</p>
                <p class="text-sm text-[var(--text-muted)] mt-0.5">{desc}</p>
              </div>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ol>

        <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3 mb-6">
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-red-500/30 bg-[var(--bg-card)] p-4 text-center">
            <p class="font-heading text-2xl font-bold text-red-500">24 hrs</p>
            <p class="text-xs text-[var(--text-muted)] mt-1">Emergency audit turnaround</p>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-red-500/30 bg-[var(--bg-card)] p-4 text-center">
            <p class="font-heading text-2xl font-bold text-red-500">~$5K</p>
            <p class="text-xs text-[var(--text-muted)] mt-1">Typical settlement with active remediation plan</p>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-red-500/30 bg-[var(--bg-card)] p-4 text-center">
            <p class="font-heading text-2xl font-bold text-red-500">$85K+</p>
            <p class="text-xs text-[var(--text-muted)] mt-1">Average judgment without remediation</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4">
          <a href="/get-quote/?service=ada-emergency" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-lg bg-red-500 px-6 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-white shadow transition hover:bg-red-600">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><line x1="12" y1="8" x2="12" y2="12"/><line x1="12" y1="16" x2="12.01" y2="16"/></svg>
            Request Emergency ADA Audit — 24-Hour Response
          </a>
          <a href="/services/ada-compliant-web-design/emergency-remediation/" class="text-sm font-semibold text-red-500 underline hover:no-underline">
            Emergency / deadline remediation: the 30-day track →
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── SECTION 2: WHAT ADA REQUIRES ────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="mb-16">
      <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl font-bold text-[var(--text)] md:text-3xl mb-4">What Does ADA Compliance Require for Your Website?</h2>
      <p class="text-[var(--text-muted)] mb-4">ADA Title III applies to "places of public accommodation." Federal courts have consistently ruled that commercial websites qualify. While no specific federal technical standard exists yet, <strong class="text-[var(--text)]">WCAG 2.1 Level AA</strong> is the de facto standard referenced by the Department of Justice and US courts.</p>
      <p class="text-[var(--text-muted)] mb-6">The DOJ's Title II final rule (effective April 24, 2026) requires government entities to meet WCAG 2.1 AA — and this sets the definitive standard the private sector will be measured against in litigation.</p>

      <h3 class="font-heading text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text)] mb-3">The 6 Most Common Violations (96% of all lawsuits)</h3>
      <ol class="space-y-2 mb-6">
        <li class="flex gap-3 rounded-lg border border-[var(--border)] bg-[var(--bg-card)] px-4 py-3 text-sm text-[var(--text-muted)]"><span class="font-bold text-red-500">1.</span><span><strong class="text-[var(--text)]">Low contrast text</strong> — 79.1% of homepages fail</span></li>
        <li class="flex gap-3 rounded-lg border border-[var(--border)] bg-[var(--bg-card)] px-4 py-3 text-sm text-[var(--text-muted)]"><span class="font-bold text-red-500">2.</span><span><strong class="text-[var(--text)]">Missing alt text on images</strong> — 55.5%</span></li>
        <li class="flex gap-3 rounded-lg border border-[var(--border)] bg-[var(--bg-card)] px-4 py-3 text-sm text-[var(--text-muted)]"><span class="font-bold text-red-500">3.</span><span><strong class="text-[var(--text)]">Missing form input labels</strong> — 48.2%</span></li>
        <li class="flex gap-3 rounded-lg border border-[var(--border)] bg-[var(--bg-card)] px-4 py-3 text-sm text-[var(--text-muted)]"><span class="font-bold text-red-500">4.</span><span><strong class="text-[var(--text)]">Empty links</strong> — 44.6%</span></li>
        <li class="flex gap-3 rounded-lg border border-[var(--border)] bg-[var(--bg-card)] px-4 py-3 text-sm text-[var(--text-muted)]"><span class="font-bold text-red-500">5.</span><span><strong class="text-[var(--text)]">Missing document language</strong> — 37.1%</span></li>
        <li class="flex gap-3 rounded-lg border border-[var(--border)] bg-[var(--bg-card)] px-4 py-3 text-sm text-[var(--text-muted)]"><span class="font-bold text-red-500">6.</span><span><strong class="text-[var(--text)]">Empty buttons</strong> — 26.3%</span></li>
      </ol>
      <p class="text-[var(--text-muted)]">At eLan Technology, we fix all of these issues as standard on every website we build. Accessibility is not an add-on — it is built into our development process from day one.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- ── SECTION 3: OUR PROCESS ──────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="mb-16">
      <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl font-bold text-[var(--text)] md:text-3xl mb-4">Our ADA Compliance Process — From Design to Deployment</h2>
      <p class="text-[var(--text-muted)] mb-8">Five rigorous steps that build accessibility into the foundation of your website — and produce the documentation needed to defend it.</p>
      <div class="grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
        {[
          { n: '1', title: 'Accessibility-First Design', items: ['Colour contrast testing during design (4.5:1 minimum)', 'Logical heading hierarchy and reading order', 'Touch targets minimum 44×44px', 'Visible focus indicators on all interactive elements', 'No information conveyed through colour alone'] },
          { n: '2', title: 'Semantic, Accessible Code', items: ['HTML5 semantic landmarks (header, nav, main, footer)', 'ARIA labels and roles where needed', 'Keyboard-navigable everything (Tab, Enter, Escape, Arrows)', 'Skip-to-content links', 'Proper form labels with error messaging'] },
          { n: '3', title: 'Content Accessibility', items: ['Alt text on every image', 'Captions and transcripts for video/audio', 'Plain-language writing at appropriate reading level', 'Descriptive link text (never "click here")'] },
          { n: '4', title: 'Testing & Validation', items: ['Automated testing with axe-core (zero violations)', 'Manual keyboard-only navigation testing', 'Screen reader testing (NVDA, VoiceOver, JAWS)', 'Lighthouse Accessibility score 95+', 'Real-user testing with assistive technology users'] },
